  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The complete short Anima Christi contains thirteen invocation or petition segments and 64 words. The first five abstract or sacramental vocatives are grammatically addressed as agents; from O BONE IESU onward Jesus is addressed directly. ME remains the same singular speaker throughout. NE PERMITTAS governs an accusative-and-infinitive construction with a passive infinitive; IUBE governs a second accusative-and-infinitive construction with an active infinitive; UT LAUDEM is the final purpose clause. No heading, attribution to Saint Ignatius, indulgence notice, surrounding Communion devotion, rubric, gesture, or vernacular enlargement belongs to the spoken text.",
